Date:   Fri Sep 25 22:50:46 2026 -0700

    Say out loud when pyproject.toml could not be parsed
    
    On Python 3.10 there is no tomllib, _toml returned {}, and the detector
    quietly installed bare "." plus pytest -- missing every test extra and
    dependency group. Tasks then failed validation as "environment problem",
    which blames the repository for what was our silence. CI on 3.10 passed
    because nothing exercised a pyproject with extras there.
    
    Now: tomllib, then tomli if installed, and if neither exists the plan
    carries a note naming the cause and the fix. A test mocks the parser
    away and asserts the note appears.
    
    Closes #36
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/groundhog/environment.py b/groundhog/environment.py
